«
@@ ============================================================
@@ ApparentSize — apparent (angular) diameter of a planet, in arcseconds
@@ Editable AstroExamples entry, companion of LightTime / Elongation.
@@ Type 1-7 (or 0 to quit), ENTER, then =. Computes today's angular diameter
@@ 2·atan(R/d): planet radius ⒸReq… over Earth-to-planet distance (DAToB), in
@@ arcseconds. Displays it and leaves Target/arcsec tagged on the stack.
@@ An invitation to build your own RPL program from the astronomy library.
@@ Author & design         : Jean Wilson
@@ Co-authors & programming : Claude & Claude Code (Anthropic)
@@ ============================================================
  DEPTH → d0
  «
    CLLCD
    "  Apparent size of a planet" 1 DISP
    "1 Mercury  2 Venus  3 Mars" 3 DISP
    "4 Jupiter  5 Saturn" 4 DISP
    "6 Uranus   7 Neptune" 5 DISP
    "0 = Quit" 6 DISP
    "Pick, ENTER, then =" 7 DISP
    HALT
    IF DEPTH d0 > THEN
      → n
      «
        IF n 0 ≠ THEN
          IF n 1 ≥ n 7 ≤ AND THEN
            DEG DateTime JDN → jd
            «
              jd Ⓛ♁Pf jd { 'Ⓛ☿Φf' 'Ⓛ♀Φf' 'Ⓛ♂Φf' 'Ⓛ♃Φf' 'Ⓛ♄Φf' 'Ⓛ⛢Φf' 'Ⓛ♆Φf' } n GET EVAL ⓁPosΦf ⓁDAToB → dist
              «
                { ⒸReq☿ ⒸReq♀ ⒸReq♂ ⒸReq♃ ⒸReq♄ ⒸReq⛢ ⒸReq♆ } n GET →Num dist 1_km CONVERT / ATAN 2 · Uval 3600 · → arcsec
                «
                  { "Mercury" "Venus" "Mars" "Jupiter" "Saturn" "Uranus" "Neptune" } n GET → name
                  «
                    CLLCD
                    "Target: " name + 1 DISP
                    "Apparent diameter:" 3 DISP
                    "  " arcsec + " arcsec" + 4 DISP
                    "Press any key" 7 DISP
                    -1 WAIT DROP
                    name "Target" →Tag
                    arcsec "arcsec" →Tag
                  »
                »
              »
            »
          ELSE
            CLLCD
            "Invalid choice." 3 DISP
            "Enter 1-7, or 0 to quit." 4 DISP
            "Press any key" 6 DISP
            -1 WAIT DROP
          END
        END
      »
    END
  »
»
